<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Professor Luther returns two weeks after his first visit, on the day of his consultation with Dr. Okafor-Lindqvist. He has kept the attack diary. He had one attack six days ago that began with roaring and fullness in the left ear, then spinning for about three hours with nausea; he lay down, took one meclizine and slept, and the roaring settled back to its usual level by the next morning. No headache, light sensitivity or visual aura came with it. He has had dull headaches on two other days, without dizziness. His mood is still low; he is sleeping five or six hours, feels guilty and joyless, and has had to push himself to write and teach. He has had no thoughts of death or of harming himself. He has never had a period of days with little need for sleep, racing thoughts or unusual energy. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Attacks</td><td>One since intake, three hours, with left-ear roaring and fullness</td></tr><tr><td>Meclizine</td><td>One dose</td></tr><tr><td>Headache</td><td>Two dull headaches without dizziness; none with the attack</td></tr><tr><td>Mood</td><td>Low, guilty, joyless; poor sleep; no thoughts of self-harm</td></tr><tr><td>Mania screen</td><td>No past hypomanic or manic episodes</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.18"/>
    <code code="10187-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Review of systems Narrative - Reported"/>
    <title>Review of Systems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Result</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Ears, nose, mouth, and throat</td><td>Positive</td><td>Constant left-ear tinnitus and fullness; muffled hearing on the left</td></tr><tr><td>Neurological</td><td>Positive</td><td>One vertigo attack; two dull headaches; no weakness, numbness, double vision or slurred speech</td></tr><tr><td>Gastrointestinal</td><td>Positive</td><td>Nausea during the attack; bowels regular</td></tr><tr><td>Genitourinary</td><td>Negative</td><td>No flank pain or blood in the urine</td></tr><tr><td>Psychiatric</td><td>Positive</td><td>Low mood, guilt, loss of interest, broken sleep; no suicidal ideation</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>5 systems reviewed. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

