    <title>Problems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>Problem</th><th>Clinical status</th><th>Verification</th><th>Code</th><th>Provenance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Recurrent attacks of spinning vertigo for about three months, the worst twelve days ago, lasting hours, with roaring tinnitus, fullness and muffled hearing in the left ear and nausea, the tinnitus persisting between attacks; with low mood, poor sleep and loss of interest; cause not established at intake: an inner-ear disorder suspected, with vestibular migraine, vestibular schwannoma and posterior circulation stroke to be excluded and depression to be assessed; otology consultation requested</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R42</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting problem anchored to his documented attacks of April and July 1527; superseded by the diagnoses at the second visit.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Ménière disease of the left ear, definite (AAO-HNS 1521 and Bárány Society criteria), with low-frequency sensorineural hearing loss and persistent tinnitus in the left ear; vestibular migraine considered and judged unlikely as the main cause; vestibular schwannoma excluded by MRI</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>H81.02</td><td>S — Synthetic modern diagnosis made at the otology consultation, linked to his documented attacks and to the retrospective diagnosis of Ménière disease (R).</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-3">
    <td>Major depressive disorder, recurrent, moderate (DSM-5-TR), with low mood, poor sleep, loss of interest, guilt and fatigue for about two months, after earlier periods of spiritual crisis and low mood; no suicidal ideation</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>F33.1</td><td>S — Synthetic modern diagnosis linked to his documented Anfechtungen and low periods; not a claim that he was so diagnosed; the retrospective psychiatric readings are disputed (R).</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-4">
    <td>Urinary stone disease: one stone passed spontaneously last year after severe pain; stone type and metabolic risk not yet known at intake</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>Z87.442</td><td>S — Synthetic modern problem anchored to his documented first stone in 1526.</td>
  </tr></tbody></table></text>

